    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No. $P(M\\cap Y)=0.25\\ne0.33=P(M)\\times P(Y)$, where $M$ means male and $Y$ means answering Yes.",
      "worked": "Let $M$ be the event that a person is male and $Y$ the event that they answered Yes.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(M\\cap Y)&=\\frac{25}{100}=0.25\\\\P(M)\\times P(Y)&=\\frac{60}{100}\\times\\frac{55}{100}\\\\P(M)\\times P(Y)&=0.33\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $P(M\\cap Y)\\ne P(M)\\times P(Y)$, attitude to the use of headgear in professional boxing is not independent of sex.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
